00:14:32,807 --> 00:14:36,817
3rd      Alan Stuart

1438
00:14:32,807 --> 00:14:36,817
3rd      Alan Stuart

1439
00:14:34,597 --> 00:14:36,817
<i>Geordo and his brother earned top scores.</i>

1440
00:14:38,217 --> 00:14:40,467
Geordo placed highest in the school, huh?

1441
00:14:40,467 --> 00:14:43,077
And you came in third, Prince Alan.

1442
00:14:43,077 --> 00:14:45,397
You're both fantastic.

1443
00:14:45,397 --> 00:14:46,827
How'd you do?

1444
00:14:47,167 --> 00:14:50,627
I'm 80th. As average as they come!

1445
00:14:50,907 --> 00:14:52,787
Uh... I see.

1446
00:14:53,347 --> 00:14:55,497
And Maria Campbell is second...

1447
00:14:56,157 --> 00:14:59,157
<i>In the game, Alan sees Maria 
as a rival after she tops his score</i>

1448
00:14:59,157 --> 00:15:01,987
<i>and picks fights with her.</i>

1449
00:15:02,287 --> 00:15:04,637
<i>And once he falls in love with her...</i>

1450
00:15:08,097 --> 00:15:10,807
Um, are you unhappy with your rank?

1451
00:15:10,957 --> 00:15:14,817
No. I don't really care 
about winning or losing.

1452
00:15:14,817 --> 00:15:17,737
People have things they're good at 
and things they're bad at,

1453
00:15:17,737 --> 00:15:19,777
so there's no point in worrying 
about every little thing.

1454
00:15:21,547 --> 00:15:26,617
Anyway, one of the teachers suggested 
I play a recital here at school.

1455
00:15:26,617 --> 00:15:27,367
What do you think?

1456
00:15:27,447 --> 00:15:29,507
That sounds great!

1457
00:15:29,507 --> 00:15:32,077
A lot of people look forward 
to hearing you play.

1458
00:15:33,737 --> 00:15:35,057
Would you...

1459
00:15:35,747 --> 00:15:37,477
Do you want to hear it, too?

1460
00:15:37,477 --> 00:15:40,287
Huh? Yes, of course!

1461
00:15:41,157 --> 00:15:42,337
Okay.

1462
00:15:42,587 --> 00:15:45,427
Then, I'll put on a recital.

